15105412,2025-08-06,Mortgage,Conventional home mortgage,Trouble during payment process,Loan sold or transferred to another company,"This complaint details a series of predatory and obstructive practices by Fay Servicing and the current loan investor concerning the property located at XXXX, NY. These actions have demonstrably jeopardized my investment, inflated my debt, and appear designed to force an unjust foreclosure. 

Background and Initial Challenges : In XXXX XXXX, our company acquired a two-family property, securing financing of XXXX XXXX through a private lender/investor, with an additional approx. {$98000.00} for planned renovations based on a scope of work. Our project was severely delayed for nearly XXXX years due to the presence of squatters and the inaccessibility of courts during the XXXX pandemic. Despite these significant obstacles, our company consistently fulfilled its mortgage obligations to the lender, often relying on personal funds and private loans to maintain payments. 

Renovation Funding Delays and Unnecessary Hurdles : Following the squatters ' eviction in XX/XX/XXXX, the original investor, despite prior awareness of the loan 's maturity and continuing to accept payments, initially refused to release the renovation funds. Only after intervention from the lender was the first draw of {$12000.00} finally received on XX/XX/XXXX, XXXX full XXXX months post-eviction. This substantial delay resulted in the loss of my construction crew and significant project setbacks. Subsequent draws on XX/XX/XXXX, and XX/XX/XXXX, were similarly difficult to obtain, requiring extensive communication and often causing payments to be processed late due to investor approval requirements. The project became a substantial drain on my personal and other business finances. 

The Transfer to Fay Servicing and XXXX  XXXX  : The situation escalated dramatically in XX/XX/XXXX, when the loan was sold to a new investor and serviced by Fay Servicing. Despite my consistent payment history with the previous investor/servicer, Fay Servicing XXXX XXXX the loan as matured and, without providing any formal notice, suggested that I apply for and extension, but refused to accept subsequent mortgage payments while an "" extension application '' was in process. I made it known that this action if prolonged, will directly manufacture a delinquency, cause delays and my company would further lose time and money. 

My attempts to resolve the situation with Fay Servicing, particularly with the Assistant Vice-President ( VP ), were met with persistent obstruction : - Forced Delinquency : Fay Servicing 's refusal to accept payments while an extension was pending directly caused the loan to become delinquent. 

- Repeated, Redundant Requests : Throughout XXXX and XX/XX/XXXX, Fay Servicing and the investor repeatedly demanded information ( e.g., updated scope of work, budget, permits, exit plan, project timeline ) that was either already provided in the initial application or could not be realistically furnished without access to the renovation funds to complete the project. For instance, a request for permits on XX/XX/XXXX, was identically repeated on XX/XX/XXXX, demonstrating a lack of internal communication or a deliberate tactic to delay. 

