15481846,2025-08-23,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Credit inquiries on your report that you don't recognize,"Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, I am submitting this complaint regarding MoneyLions inaccurate and damaging reporting to the credit bureaus. 

MoneyLion is reporting 30 and 60day late payments on an account that was already closed. This account was closed after nonpayment, but I later paid enough to settle and cancel it out. After the closure and settlement, there should be no further reporting of late payments because no active account or obligation exists. 

Despite this, MoneyLion continues to add late payment notations to my credit file as if the account were still open. This is both misleading and harmful, as it is negatively affecting my credit score. 

I believe this conduct violates the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), which requires furnishers to report information that is accurate and not misleading. Reporting late payments after an account is closed and settled is inaccurate and unlawful. 

I respectfully request that the CFPB : 1. Investigate MoneyLions improper reporting practices.

2. Require MoneyLion to immediately remove all inaccurate late payment notations from my credit file.

3. Ensure that they cease reporting any further negative activity on a closed account.

I can provide supporting documentation of my payments and settlement upon request.

