3. PRA is attempting to collect on an alleged online account but has failed to show proof that I opened or authorized such an account. Without authentication ( such as original application records, IP logs, or contract ), they can not lawfully establish that I am responsible.

Harm This inaccurate reporting has damaged my creditworthiness, interfered with my ability to obtain credit on fair terms, and caused unnecessary stress and hardship.

Requested Resolution I respectfully request that the CFPB : 1. Investigate PRAs failure to properly validate the alleged debt.

2. Require PRA to cease all collection activity and delete this account from my credit reports unless they can produce concrete documentation that the debt is valid and was lawfully created by me.

3. Ensure compliance with FDCPA and FCRA provisions regarding proper debt verification and fair credit reporting. 



Thank you for your attention to this matter. Please contact me if you require additional documentation. 

Sincerely, XXXX",,"Portfolio Recovery Associates, LLC",FL,328XX,,Web,2025-08-31,Closed with explanation,Yes
